    description: "Source: deep-20260407-030917 kserve reflect agent question. The python.yaml library_patterns currently covers .append/.extend/.add/.update/.write/.send/.put/.read/.recv/.get/.keys/.values/.items/.pop/.remove/.clear/.discard/.popitem/.flush/.writelines (~20 patterns). Suggested extensions: open (read or write depending on mode arg, default read), close (delete?), seek (mutate), truncate (delete/write), readline/readlines (read), json.dump/json.load (write/read), json.dumps/json.loads (read), pickle.dump/pickle.load (write/read), yaml.dump/yaml.load (write/read). These are common Python data-handling primitives that currently leave call edges unannotated. Note: per WI-saful needs_human_review, the dataflow slice may not currently consume read edges anyway, so the immediate impact is on access_mode_coverage metric and the per-edge tagging visible in dataflow output."  # 192d
